{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And they performed the pesaḥ.</b> Rabbi Yosi says: Israel did not perform a pesaḥ in the wilderness except that one alone. And the reason is that at that time they were encamped in one place and were able to circumcise the males born to them, so that their circumcision would not prevent them from eating the pesaḥ. But from then onward, when they journeyed in the wilderness, they did not circumcise the children born to them because of the weakness of the road and the danger to one circumcised on the way, as it is written: וכל העם הילודים במדבר בדרך בצאתם מארץ מצרים לא מלו — and the foreskin of his males prevents him from eating the pesaḥ, as it is written: המול לו כל זכר ואז יקרב לעשותו — therefore they did not perform the pesaḥ. And our Rabbis said: because all the forty years that Israel were in the wilderness, no north wind blew for them, and they had no sunny day for circumcision."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:17:07.139015760Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}